// Detection: Windows Event Log Cleared
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1070.001 (Indicator Removal: Clear Windows Event Logs)
// Log source: Microsoft Sentinel — SecurityEvent (forwarded via AMA/MMA)
//
// What it detects:
//   Event ID 1102 (audit log cleared) or 104 (System log cleared) —
//   both are rare in normal operations and are a textbook anti-forensic
//   step taken immediately after other malicious activity.
//
// Why it matters:
//   Clearing logs is almost never done by accident and almost always
//   happens right after something the attacker doesn't want you to
//   see. Because the technique erases the very evidence you'd use to
//   investigate, this alert should trigger immediate review of any
//   other activity from the same host/account in the preceding hour.
//
// False positive considerations:
//   - Scheduled log archival/rotation jobs on some servers legitimately
//     clear logs after export — confirm your log management tooling's
//     service account and exclude it explicitly, not by broad process
//     name.
//   - This should be a near-zero-false-positive, high-severity alert in
//     most environments; investigate every hit rather than tuning it
//     down.

SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1d)
| where EventID in (1102, 104)
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, Account, EventID, Activity
| order by TimeGenerated desc
